<h1>Show Command Window</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>Modules &gt; Macros &gt; <i style="font-weight:bold;">Show</i></b></i><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Command Window</b></span></span> or by pressing <b>F11.</b></p>
<p class="Description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> The <i style="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal;">Show Command Window</i> displays or hides the log window where macro commands are stored after their execution.</p>
<p><img src="../Images/Command_window.gif" width="629px" height="383px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p>Command Window can be docked to the bottom side of KUBE application window (above the Status Bar) ot to the top side (below the toolbar). This is done when enable <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Dock</b></span> mode from <span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>Modules &gt; Macros &gt; Dock</b></i></span> or from the <span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>context menu of Command Window &gt; Dock</b></i></span>.</p>
<p><img src="../Images/Command_window2.gif" width="929px" height="472px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p class="bullet">The edit field on the bottom of the window is for typing commands. After pressing Enter key the command is executed. If a command has parameters there are two ways of calling it:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">By typing the command’s name only. If the command has parameters its dialog box appears so you can set the parameters.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="margin-left:64px;">For example:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="margin-left:64px;">Type <font style="font-family:Courier New;" face="Courier New">FillHoles</font> and press Enter.<br>
Fill Holes dialog appear.<br>
Now tune the parameters and press OK to execute this function.</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="margin-left:64px;"><img src="../Images/Command_window1.gif" width="629px" height="383px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
<ol start="2">
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">By typing the whole command with its parameters.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="margin-left:64px;">For example if we want to execute Fill Holes with the parameters in the upper example, we need to type the following:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="margin-left:64px;">FillHoles( Method="CrvBased", LimitEdges=Yes, MaxEdges=50 )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="margin-left:64px;">&#160;</p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">Please, note that the macro commands and their parameters are not case sensitive. It means that FillHoles, fillholes, and FILLHOLES have the same meaning.</span></p>
